From: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 21:13:47 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mt7996: size the host token range from the NPU
 token count

An NPU tx token is an index into the tx-pkt reserved memory region,
2 KiB per token, so the count the driver hands the NPU firmware must
match a reservation the driver cannot see. The NPU driver reads the
count from the device tree, checks it against the reservation and
exports it; the host token range starts above that count. A device
tree without the count falls back to the compile-time count.

A TX free event carries a 15-bit MSDU ID with the top value reserved,
so a host token ID of 32767 or above never returns and aliases to a
lower ID. The host pool shrinks until every host token ID fits, with
a warning that names both counts, because the device tree sets the
NPU count per board. A count that leaves no host token fails the NPU
setup. WED keeps its own token layout: it is a different offload
engine with its own buffers and is not used on the AN7581.

Based-on-work-by: monish.v <monish.v>
Signed-off-by: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
---
 mt7996/npu.c |   21 +++++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 19 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/mt7996/npu.c
+++ b/mt7996/npu.c
@@ -7,6 +7,7 @@
 #include <linux/soc/airoha/airoha_offload.h>
 
 #include "mt7996.h"
+#include "mac.h"
 
 static int mt7992_npu_txrx_offload_init(struct mt7996_dev *dev,
 					struct airoha_npu *npu)
@@ -200,6 +201,7 @@ static int mt7996_npu_txrx_offload_init(
 static int mt7996_npu_offload_init(struct mt7996_dev *dev,
 				   struct airoha_npu *npu)
 {
+	u32 token_size = npu->tx_token_num ?: MT7996_HW_TOKEN_SIZE;
 	u32 val;
 	int err;
 
@@ -229,12 +231,27 @@ static int mt7996_npu_offload_init(struc
 	if (err)
 		return err;
 
+	/* a 15-bit MSDU ID in the TX free event; the top value is reserved */
+	if (token_size >= MT_TXFREE_INFO_MSDU_ID) {
+		dev_err(dev->mt76.dev,
+			"%u NPU tx tokens leave no host tx token ID\n", token_size);
+		return -EINVAL;
+	}
+
 	err = mt76_npu_send_msg(npu, 0, WLAN_FUNC_SET_WAIT_TOKEN_ID_SIZE,
-				MT7996_HW_TOKEN_SIZE, GFP_KERNEL);
+				token_size, GFP_KERNEL);
 	if (err)
 		return err;
 
-	dev->mt76.token_start = MT7996_HW_TOKEN_SIZE;
+	spin_lock_bh(&dev->mt76.token_lock);
+	dev->mt76.token_start = token_size;
+	if (token_size + dev->mt76.token_size > MT_TXFREE_INFO_MSDU_ID) {
+		dev->mt76.token_size = MT_TXFREE_INFO_MSDU_ID - token_size;
+		dev_warn(dev->mt76.dev,
+			 "%u NPU tx tokens leave %u host tx tokens\n",
+			 token_size, dev->mt76.token_size);
+	}
+	spin_unlock_bh(&dev->mt76.token_lock);
 
 	return 0;
 }
